# Captured tool output is compared by SHA-256 over the raw bytes, so a
# checkout that rewrote line endings would break every digest while leaving the
# content semantically unchanged. Pinning these to LF keeps the captures
# byte-identical on every platform; without it the failure would look like a
# fabricated capture on Windows.
#
# "text eol=lf" and not "-text eol=lf": the leading dash marks the file binary
# and disables conversion, which lets CRLF through unchanged and is the
# opposite of what is wanted here. Verified with git check-attr and by
# inspecting the staged bytes.
workflow/tests/fixtures/tool-contracts/** text eol=lf
